! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F208A "ADD DOUBLE TEST
! ROUTINE -- ARITHMETIC CHECKS", the whole routine, A1-A20
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf pp.93-96, octal
! 014613.00-015026.40, where the listing's own exit sequence
! BD,$+1.0 / B,FAD1 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW begins): the
! exercise of D+ -- the first double-precision ARITHMETIC the model
! can do.
!
! Each sub-test builds a full 96-bit double-precision value in the
! accumulator and adds a storage operand to it:
!   DL(U) puts a word into bits 0-59 and clears 60-107; where the
!     comment says "+ 48", a C0011 of another constant's fraction
!     (48 bits at .12) into accumulator offset 20 fills the low half,
!     so the accumulator holds a genuine 96-bit fraction rather than
!     one padded with zeros;
!   D+(U) adds a storage operand, which the machine extends with 48
!     low-order zeros (Ref. Manual p.95);
!   then three checks -- the low order fraction (48 bits at offset
!     20), the high order fraction (48 bits at offset 68) and the
!     exponent (12 bits at offset 116) -- and, where a carry out of
!     the 48 high-order bits is expected, BZLC.
!
! What that exercises, and could not be exercised before: the carry
! ACROSS the halves. A2 and A4 add a value to itself with the
! accumulator's low half non-zero, so the low half overflows into the
! high half and (A2, A4) out of the top, which is what the BZLC
! checks; A1/A3/A5/A7 place the operand 48 places up so the
! preparatory shift crosses the half boundary. A single-precision
! adder cannot produce any of these results.
!
! A10-A14 take the operands into the XFP and XFN ranges, where the
! result is one operand WHOLE rather than a sum -- so they check 60
! bits at offset 68 (exponent and high fraction together) and 48 at
! offset 20, with no exponent check of their own and no carry to look
! for. What they add over the single-precision flagged tests is the
! low half: A10 and A12 carry a non-zero low half through a flagged
! add untouched, and A11/A14 require the SURVIVING operand's low half
! -- zero, since a storage operand is extended with zeros -- to
! replace whatever was there. FK35, whose fraction is zero, is what
! those checks compare against.
!
! A15-A19 are the "TEST NORMALIZATION MODIFIER" section, D+(N).
! A15-A18 keep a FLAGGED operand as the survivor, so normalization is
! suppressed and the listing's comment is "error if result
! normalized". A19 is the one that normalizes: an N-range accumulator
! (+13, with FPK4's fraction filling its low half) surviving an XFN
! operand, so the whole 96-bit fraction shifts left and the exponent
! follows it. That is the first double-precision normalization the
! model performs -- fpNormalize96Wide over 96 real bits rather than 48
! padded with zeros -- and FPK3/FPK15 are its two halves.
!
! A20 onward (from 015016.00) is not transcribed here; this program's
! PASS sits exactly where it begins, which is what checks that every
! word length before it is right.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. The prologue
! (014607.40, the SSIP routine identification) is not transcribed; the
! block starts at the "B,$+.32" ahead of F208A1. Constants from the
! pool pp.176 and 178.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), C0011 into the accumulator at offset 20,
! D+(U), CT0110 over 60-, 48- and 12-bit fields at offsets 20/68/116,
! BZLC, SIC, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f208a_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: all twenty passed on the first run of a freshly written
! 96-bit adder, which is a stronger statement than it sounds -- the
! low-order checks are sensitive to every bit of the preparatory shift
! and the carry across the halves. Two injections show the two halves
! of the block bite separately:
!   - making D+ read only the accumulator's high 48 bits and pad with
!     zeros, which is what a single-precision adder sees, halts at
!     014617.40, A1's low order fraction check -- the first check in
!     the block;
!   - making the FLAGGED path drop the surviving operand's low half
!     halts at 014732.00, A10's low order check, while A1-A9 still
!     pass. That one is worth having: the flagged path returns an
!     operand whole rather than computing anything, so nothing in
!     A1-A9 would have noticed it losing 48 bits.
!   - A20 reaches a third place: it is the only sub-test in the
!     routine that normalizes on the UNFLAGGED path. Every earlier
!     D+(N) -- A15 through A19 -- has a flagged operand, so its
!     normalization runs in the flagged branch instead, and A1-A18's
!     D+(U) does not normalize at all. Dropping the normalization
!     exponent adjustment on the unflagged branch therefore halts at
!     A20's own exponent check (SIC stores 015022.40, the half-word
!     after the BRGZ that guards the CT0110(BU,12) at 015020.40) with
!     A1-A19 still passing.
!
! A20 is also the routine's only isolated exponent check: 12 bits at
! accumulator offset 116 (IBM 0-11), with the fraction checked as two
! separate 48-bit fields at offsets 68 (IBM 12-59) and 20 (IBM
! 60-107), where every earlier flagged sub-test folds exponent and
! high fraction together into one 60-bit check at 68. Its arithmetic
! sits exactly on the PSH boundary -- the exponents differ by 48, so
! the operand shifts out of the high half into the low half exactly --
! and the 12-place normalization then pulls bits back across that
! boundary, 50 - 12 = 38 being the exponent FK101 checks.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22030.0
FPK19   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000525252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)22044.0
FPK31   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000000000000000000
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
FPK33   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777740
FPK34   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001000000000000000020
FPK35   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001125252525252525240
FPK36   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252500
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
FPK39   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22007.0
FPK2    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22173.0
FK25    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22200.0
FK30    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577617777777777777760
FK31    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777612525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22204.0
FK34    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0200377777777777777770
FK35    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777400000000000000000
FK36    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1000177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22210.0
FK38    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0777572525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22220.0
FK46    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1746577777777777777760
FK47    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000017777777777760
FK48    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0030177777777777600000
        SLC, (8)22010.0
FPK3    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525240
FPK4    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000452525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22023.0
FPK14   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0006400005252525252520
FPK15   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252400000
        SLC, (8)22174.0
FK26    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777412525252525252520
FK27    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577405252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22211.0
FK39    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0777625252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22306.0
FK101   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0023177777777777600000

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)14613.0
DAD1A   B, $+.32   ! F208A1: exp. mem + 48 + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FPK32
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK33+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK34+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK31, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A2: exp. mem + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK21
        D+(U), FPK21
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK33+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BZLC, SERS   ! to check for the high order carry
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK21, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A3: exp. mem + 48 + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK19+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FPK35
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK36+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK34+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK31, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A4: exp. mem + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK37
        D+(U), FPK37
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK36+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BZLC, SERS   ! to check for the high order carry
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK37, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A5: exp. mem + 48 + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK38+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FPK39
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK31, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A6: exp. mem + exp. acc.
        DL(U), FPK38
        D+(U), FPK38
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK38, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FPK31   ! F208A7: exp mem + exp acc ++48
        C0011(BU,48), FPK36+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FPK35
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK33+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK31, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A8: exp.mem+exp.acc
        DL(U), FPK38
        D+(U), FPK37
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK31+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK38, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A9: exp.acc+48+exp.mem
        DL(U), FPK32
        D+(U), FPK21
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 20   ! test low order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK21+.12, 68   ! test high order fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,12), FPK21, 116   ! test exponent + 50
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FK35   ! F208A10: exps in XFP range
        C0011(BU,48), FK34+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FK46
        CT0110(BU,60), FK35, 68   ! test result + opnd
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK34+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A11: exponents of opnds in XFP and N ranges
        DL(U), FK36
        D+(U), FK38
        CT0110(BU,60), FK36, 68   ! test result + opnd
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A12: exponents of opnds in XFP and XFN ranges
        DL(U), FK35
        C0011(BU,48), FK34+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FK25
        CT0110(BU,60), FK35, 68   ! test result + opnd
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK34+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A13: exponents of opnds in N and XFN ranges
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(U), FPK2
        CT0110(BU,60), FPK31, 68   ! test result + opnd
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FK31   ! F208A14: exps in XFN range
        D+(U), FK30
        CT0110(BU,60), FK30, 68   ! test result + opnd
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A15: exponents of opnds in XFP range
        DL(U), FK26
        D+(N), FK27   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,60), FK26, 68   ! error if result normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A16: exponents of opnds in XFP and N ranges
        DL(U), FK26
        D+(N), FK39   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,60), FK26, 68   ! error if result normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A17: exponents of opnds in XFP and XFN ranges
        DL(U), FK26
        D+(N), FK30   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,60), FK26, 68   ! error if result normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A18: exponents of opnds in XFN range
        DL(U), FK31
        D+(N), FK30   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,60), FK30, 68   ! error if result normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK35+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A19: exponents of opnds in N and XFN ranges
        DL(U), FPK14
        C0011(BU,48), FPK4+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(N), FPK2   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,60), FPK3, 68   ! error if result not normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FPK15+.12, 20   ! and its low order half
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F208A20: exponents of opnds in N range
        DL(U), FK47
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20   ! set the accumulator's low half
        D+(N), FPK39   ! normalized
        CT0110(BU,12), FK101, 116   ! the result exponent -- result normalized
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK46+.12, 68   ! IBM 12-59 of the fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0110(BU,48), FK48+.12, 20   ! and IBM 60-107
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                  ! 015026.40: F208A exits here
        END, DAD1A
